Third-party components, none of which are bundled here:

  numpy            BSD 3-Clause
  sounddevice      MIT
  PortAudio        MIT
  espeak-ng        GPL-3.0-or-later   (optional speech engine)
  piper-tts        MIT                (optional speech engine)
  onnxruntime      MIT                (required by piper-tts)

A note on espeak-ng, because it matters for anyone shipping this in a product:
it is GPL-3.0-or-later, and GPLv3's anti-tivoization terms require that users
be able to run modified versions on the device. Many hardware manufacturers
will not accept that. This project does not depend on espeak-ng — the speech
engine sits behind a deliberately small interface so it can be replaced. Piper
(MIT) and Flite (BSD) are drop-in alternatives.
